# Knowledge-AI Project Rules

## Layout

- Monorepo: `api/` (FastAPI backend), `client/` (React SPA, Week 15+)
- Do not commit `knowledge-ai-project-brief.md` (gitignored, local only)
- Read `PROGRESS.md` at repo root for current week and handoff state

## Backend architecture (`api/`)

- Controller–service separation:
  - `api/v1/*.py` — thin HTTP handlers
  - `services/*.py` — business logic
  - `models/*.py` — SQLAlchemy ORM
  - `schemas/*.py` — Pydantic DTOs
- Use `Depends(get_db)` for DB sessions; do not use global middleware for JWT auth
- Postgres enums: always use `values_callable=str_enum_values` from `models/base.py`

## Domain naming

- Stored documents: **KnowledgeNeuron**, **Command**
- MCP aggregated output: **StratumContext** (built by `ContextBuilder`)
- Never use "pill" terminology

## Stack

- Python 3.12+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy async, Alembic, PostgreSQL + pgvector, Redis, Celery (later)
- Package manager: `uv` | Author: Henry Merchan <merchanha@gmail.com>

## Workflow

- Docs-first: write `api/docs/NN-*.md` before pushing each week
- Run `ruff check .`, `mypy .`, `pytest` in `api/` before commits
- Migrations: `uv run alembic upgrade head` after model changes

## Testing locally

- Only one uvicorn on port 8000 (`lsof -i :8000` if routes missing)
- Health: `/api/v1/health` | Readiness: `/api/v1/health/ready`
